EN 16931-1 attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is an implementation of the semantic data model of EN 16931-1:2017+A1:2019/
AC:2020 (Electronic invoicing - Part 1: Semantic data model of the core elements
of an electronic invoice) and, for the cross industry invoice, of one of the two
mandatory syntaxes of EN 16931-2; the universal business language is read but not
yet written. Such reproduction is granted with the permission of CEN and the
relevant member national standardisation bodies as copyright owners.

CEN and the relevant member national standardisation bodies bear no liability
from the content and implementation of such derivative applications and, in case
of doubt, users shall always refer to the official authoritative content of the
semantic data model and two mandatory syntaxes.

The English text of EN 16931-1 was accessed free of charge through the national
standards body Úrad pre normalizáciu, metrológiu a skúšobníctvo Slovenskej
republiky (ÚNMS SR), under the licence agreement between the European Commission
and CEN of 18 December 2018.

No normative prose of EN 16931-1 is reproduced in this repository. The files here
carry business term identifiers, cardinalities, data type names and paraphrased
descriptions written for this project, and they cite the clauses of the standard
rather than quoting them. See docs/sources.md for how to obtain the text.

Where this distribution carries the term registry model/en16931/2026.json, this
project also implements EN 16931-1:2026, the 2026 edition of that standard, in
that registry and in the artefacts generated from it. The file
model/en16931/2026.paths lists those files; a distribution built without them
carries no registry of that edition, and this paragraph then describes nothing
that is shipped. The text of that edition is not available free of charge: it was
obtained as a copy bought from a national standards body, it is not redistributed
here, and no prose of it is reproduced. The licence agreement named above is
documented for the 2017 version of the standard and is to be renegotiated on
revision, so this project claims no CEN permission for the 2026 edition. The
publisher of this project decided to distribute those files as what they are:
the identifiers, cardinalities and data types an implementation needs in order
to run, in this project's own words, with no text of the standard and none of
its processes. CEN and the national standards bodies give no warranty for this
implementation, and where this project and the standard disagree, the standard
governs.

